## Summary
This article discusses potential changes to the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) in 2020, noting that regulators have been active in enforcement. It mentions that hundreds of fines, totaling over €114 million, were issued to companies like Google and Facebook in the first 20 months since GDPR's implementation.

## Key Points
- GDPR regulators have been actively enforcing the regulation.
- Hundreds of fines have been imposed on companies, including major tech firms.
- Total fines exceeded €114 million within the first 20 months of GDPR.
- The article explores anticipated changes to GDPR regulations for 2020.
- Major companies such as Google and Facebook have been targeted by fines.


